# Muxiz Full-Stack Music Platform Architecture & Guidelines

## 1. Core Architecture
- **Mobile (Flutter)**:
  - State: `flutter_riverpod` (StateNotifierProvider, NotifierProvider)
  - Audio Engine: `just_audio` + `audio_service` with single `ConcatenatingAudioSource`
  - Real-time Sync: `RemoteSyncService` connects to server SSE `/api/server/events` and updates `MockMusicCatalog` with zero playback interruption.
  - User Sync: Automatically syncs active mobile profile via `POST /api/v1/users`.
- **Backend & Cloud Vault (Node.js Express in `server/`)**:
  - Vault: Google Drive 5TB with HTTP 206 Range Stream Proxy (`/api/v1/songs/stream/:fileId`).
  - Database: MongoDB Atlas + `LocalStore` zero-downtime cache fallback (`server/data/`).
  - Apple Music Engine: Auto-extracts official track metadata & 1400x1400 Ultra HD artwork (`metadataService.js`).
  - Studio Admin Console: React + Vite + Tailwind clean white theme (`server/client/`).

## 2. Audio Pipeline & Real-Time Sync Rules
- Never create duplicate `AudioPlayer` instances.
- Audio stream requests must support `Accept-Ranges: bytes` and `Content-Range`.
- Studio Admin actions (upload, edit, delete, cache wipe) must bump the global cache epoch and broadcast SSE `catalog_update`.
- Mobile cache updates must refresh catalog silently in background without killing or pausing active audio streams.

## 3. User & Artist Data Policies
- Zero dummy/mock users: Users are strictly registered from the Flutter frontend mobile app.
- Artists are normalized and deduplicated across tracks with exact track counts.
- Strict ID-based song deletion with cascading orphan cleanup for artists/albums with 0 remaining tracks.

## 4. UI/UX Standards
- **Studio Console**: Apple & Linear inspired Clean White Theme (`#ffffff`, `#f8fafc`, `#e2e8f0`), official `app_logo.png`, zero neon glowing effects.
- **Mobile App**: Dark theme (`#121212`), high contrast, floating mini player, gesture swipe, lock-screen media controls.
